onal flu and  suggesting we have learned to live with  it  and should do the same with covet 19. a  sign he plans to portray himself as a  strong man against a pandemic that has  killed 210  000 americans we have essentially  politics  infecting our public's health this is a  disaster for public health in general  it's also now a national security threat  at the pentagon  seven senior military leaders including  the chairman of the joint chiefs of  staff  are in quarantine after their own  exposure several of them had been at the  white house for this maskless indoor  ceremony on september 27th  the day after that now infamous rose  garden event  there are more cases coming out of the  white house these days than  in entire other countries and that's  simple because  we're not choosing to fight this and  democrat choosing to accommodate it  incredibly the white house with all its  resources has refused to undertake  contact tracing or notification  even as cases now spike in washington  d.c  the administration is also refusing to  give any information about the  president's  own history of testing if we need to be  taking samples those  swabs that have diagnosed them as  positive have  very important information that could  tell us exactly how this virus was  introduced  into the white house and that genetic  information could  could be used to explain exactly  who transmitted it to whom  the president's defiance of the virus  comes as polls show him slipping even  further behind joe biden one survey out  today has him  16 points behind at the same time though  there's still a strategy to try and  carry on with the presidential debates  the president says  he will travel to the next one although  there's likely to be a squabble over  debate preventative measures surrounding  covid19  tomorrow's vice presidential debate has  already descended into a bit of a  squabble  over whether or not the candidate should  be protected behind plexiglas screens  donna okay lots to