ic]  the canadian flag and an escort of  mounties an image  so befitting a man admired above all  else for his love of country  john turner's funeral brought  dignitaries from his days in politics  friends he'd had for life and family  jill's to whom he was married for 57  years  we have lost our northern star to his  daughter elizabeth turner set an example  with his dignity  friends spoke of the great outdoorsmen  his generosity  his humor when john heard people  complain about the weather  he would say come on are you a tourist  or a canadian  justin trudeau has known john turner  since he was a child  today more than ever we need more people  like john  his legacy calls on us not to wait for  change to happen  but to stand up and build a better  country  for everyone we'll carry our share of  the load and we will  john turner seemed destined for  leadership he was charismatic  he'd qualified for the olympics and was  a rhodes scholar  as a young lawyer he had a relationship  with princess margaret that seemed  briefly  serious he turned to politics recruited  by lester pearson's liberals  then served in the cabinet of another  rising star pierre trudeau  for turner politics was an honorable  calling to build a better nation  i've avoided what i like to call  cosmetic politics  the type of politics that look good in  the short term but wouldn't be  good for the country after a dispute  with trudeau over campaign promises  turner left politics for almost a decade  but then came back for the job  he'd always wanted turner one  thousand eight hundred and sixty-two  turner  he out dueled jean-critician for the  liberal leadership and in 1984 became  canada's  17th prime minister it lasted 79 days  patronage appointments left to him by  trudeau led to a defining blow by brian  mulroney in an election debate  you had an option sir you could have  said i am not going to do it this is  wrong for canada  may i congratulate mr mulroney the  liberals suffered one of their worst  electoral defeats  in the next election he tried again  debating free trade  i happen to believe that you've sold us  out a champion of canadian sovereignty  turner would not however win back the  job of prime minister  over the years i've found that the  goodbyes in this place are far more  generous and spontaneous than the hello  democracy does not happen by accident  become  involved get out there  get something back  state funerals are rare but this was  unique in the time of covet 19  so many more would have wished to be  here to honor a man who did indeed  give something back  [Music]  the funeral of john turner that is  global national for this tuesday i'm  donna friesen tonight's your canada is  near maycroft in southwestern alberta  there are beautiful spots all over this  country please email us yours to viewers  at globalnational.com  thanks for watching hope to see you here  again tomorrow take care of yourselves  [Music]  bye-bye
 

